ready: 1
kind: journey
id: recall.session
display_id: FLOW-RECALL-SESSION
module: recall
actors: [actor.agent, actor.owner]
title: Memory during an agent session
summary: The agent receives a memory index at the start, cues beside prompts, gut checks before risky actions, and uses recall tools as it works.
trigger: A session starts in a connected runtime, or the agent loads its memory
steps:
  - recall.session.start
  - recall.session.prompt
  - recall.session.plan-tool
  - recall.session.warned
  - recall.session.paused
  - recall.session.search
  - recall.session.feedback
  - recall.session.checkpoint
  - recall.session.end
sequences:
  - recall.seq.session-index
  - recall.seq.load
  - recall.seq.cue
  - recall.seq.gut-check
  - recall.seq.search
  - recall.seq.feedback
  - recall.seq.checkpoint
rationale: >-
  With nothing to say, Kernle adds nothing: empty preambles and no-memory
  messages would cost context in every session. Codex has no hooks, so its
  sessions use only the tool path from the search step on.
